  QuizId: quiz_breathing
  ModuleId: breathing
  Title: Breathing In & Out
  Questions:
  - Question: Air travels to the lungs through the...
    Options:
    - Trachea
    - Esophagus
    - Aorta
    - Spine
    CorrectIndex: 0
    Explanation: The trachea (windpipe) carries air toward the lungs.
  - Question: The trachea branches into two tubes called the...
    Options:
    - Bronchi
    - Alveoli
    - Arteries
    - Valves
    CorrectIndex: 0
    Explanation: The bronchi lead into the left and right lungs.
  - Question: When you inhale, your chest cavity...
    Options:
    - Expands
    - Shrinks
    - Stays the same
    - Collapses
    CorrectIndex: 0
    Explanation: The chest expands to draw air into the lungs.
